  "reading": {
   "title": "A recipe from Hafsa",
   "text": "Hafsa shares a recipe with Linda. It is for Turkish lentil soup. \"You need a cup of red lentils, one onion, a little butter, some salt and water,\" she says. \"It isn't hard.\"\n\n\"First, slice the onion. Then put the butter in a pot and add the onion. Cook for five minutes. Next, add the lentils and a lot of water. Boil for twenty minutes. Add a little salt at the end.\"\n\nLinda asks, \"How many onions do I need?\" \"Just one,\" says Hafsa. \"And don't add too much salt. A little is enough.\"\n\nOn Sunday, Linda makes a big pot of soup. She eats it with bread. \"It's delicious!\" she says. \"Can I have the recipe for your cake, too?\"",
   "glossary": [
